      "content": "# Actions\n\n## Overview\n\nActions are the business logic implementations mapped to extension operations. Each action receives `InputFields` and returns `ActionOutput`.\n\n## File: src/actions/__init__.py\n\n```python\nfrom actions.output import ActionOutput\n\n# Import your action functions\nfrom actions.create_resource import create_resource\nfrom actions.delete_resource import delete_resource\n\n# Map action names to functions\nACTION_MAPPER = {\n    \"create\": create_resource,\n    \"delete\": delete_resource\n}\n```\n\n## Action Function Signature\n\n**Action functions ONLY accept `input_data: InputFields`**\n\n```python\nfrom fields import InputFields\nfrom actions import ActionOutput\nfrom manager import ExtensionManager\nfrom exceptions import ExecutionError\n\n\nextension_manager = ExtensionManager()\ndef my_action(input_data: InputFields) -> ActionOutput:\n    \"\"\"\n    Action implementation.\n\n    **IMPORTANT: Actions ONLY take input_data parameter - OutputFields is created inside the function!**\n\n    Args:\n        input_data: Validated input fields (ONLY parameter!)\n\n    Returns:\n        ActionOutput with results\n    \"\"\"\n    # Check cancellation\n    if extension_manager.is_cancelled():\n        raise OperationCancelledError(\"Cancelled\")\n\n    # Perform operation\n    result = perform_operation(input_data)\n\n    # Return output\n    return ActionOutput(\n        resource_id=result.id,\n        resource_name=result.name,\n        details={\"status\": \"success\"}\n    )\n```\n\n## OutputFields Usage (Real-time UI Updates)\n\n\nUse OutputFields for progress tracking and status updates:\n\n```python\nfrom fields.output import OutputFields\n\ndef process_items_action(input_data: InputFields) -> ActionOutput:\n    # 1. Create and initialize OutputFields\n    output_fields = OutputFields(\n        status=\"Starting\",\n        progress=\"0%\",\n        items_processed=0\n    )\n\n    # 2. Access previous run data if needed